<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<rdf:RDF
  xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/"
  xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
  xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
  xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
  xmlns:vann="http://purl.org/vocab/vann/"
>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://schema.org/version">
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The version of the DigitalObject.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>schema:version</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://schema.org/identifier">
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The identifier property represents any kind of identifier for any kind of Thing, such as ISBNs, GTIN codes, UUIDs etc. Schema.org provides dedicated properties for representing many of these, either as textual strings or as URL (URI) links.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>schema:identifier</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:Ontology rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <owl:versionIRI rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI/1.6"/>
    <owl:priorVersion rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI/1.5"/>
    <owl:backwardCompatibleWith rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI/1.5"/>
    <owl:versionInfo xml:lang="en">1.6</owl:versionInfo>
    <dcterms:title xml:lang="en">EVI: Evidence Graph Ontology</dcterms:title>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">The Evidence Graph ontology extends core concepts from the W3C Provenance Ontology PROV-O, Schema.org, and Bioschemas' Profiles to describe evidence for correctness of findings in biomedical publications. The semantic data model in EVI is expressed using OWL2 Web Ontology Language (OWL2).</dcterms:description>
    <dcterms:created xml:lang="en">2020-07-27</dcterms:created>
    <dcterms:modified xml:lang="en">2026-08-13</dcterms:modified>
    <dcterms:license rdf:resource="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"/>
    <dcterms:creator>
      <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4647-3877">
        <rdfs:label>Sadnan Al Manir</rdfs:label>
      </owl:NamedIndividual>
    </dcterms:creator>
    <dcterms:creator>
      <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4060-7360">
        <rdfs:label>Timothy Clark</rdfs:label>
      </owl:NamedIndividual>
    </dcterms:creator>
    <dcterms:contributor rdf:resource="https://github.com/jniestroy"/>
    <dcterms:contributor rdf:resource="https://github.com/mlev71"/>
    <vann:preferredNamespacePrefix>evi</vann:preferredNamespacePrefix>
    <vann:preferredNamespaceUri rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#"/>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://fairscape.github.io/EVI/"/>
  </owl:Ontology>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#parametersCount">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#MLModel"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The number of variables a model learns during training. For current LLM models, this number ranges from millions to trillions that determines the performance and complexity of these models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>parametersCount</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#directlyChallengedBy">
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf>
      <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#challengedBy">
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#challenges"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Reverse of challenges property.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>challengedBy</rdfs:label>
      </owl:ObjectProperty>
    </rdfs:subPropertyOf>
    <owl:inverseOf>
      <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#directlyChallenges">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#challenges"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#DigitalObject"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#DigitalObject"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The directlyChallenges property establishes a relation between instances of DigitalObjects A and B when A asserts that B is wrong or deficient. It is non-transitive, entailing indirectlyChallenges properties on DigitalObjects supportedBy the DigitalObject it directlyChallenges, via a property chain rule.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>directlyChallenges</rdfs:label>
      </owl:ObjectProperty>
    </owl:inverseOf>
    <rdfs:comment>Reverse of directlyChallenges property.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>directlyChallengedBy</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://schema.org/dateCreated">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Dataset"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Date when the item was created.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>schema:dateCreated</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#reagentUsedBy">
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf>
      <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#usedBy">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#directlySupports"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Reverse of used property.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>usedBy</rdfs:label>
      </owl:ObjectProperty>
    </rdfs:subPropertyOf>
    <owl:inverseOf>
      <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#usedReagent">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#used"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Experiment"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Reagent"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The property usedReagent is a subproperty of used where domain is Experiment and range is Reagent.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>usedReagent</rdfs:label>
      </owl:ObjectProperty>
    </owl:inverseOf>
    <rdfs:comment>Reverse of usedReagent property.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>reagentUsedBy</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://schema.org/description">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A description of the item.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>schema:description</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://schema.org/Dataset">
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Dataset"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#DigitalObject"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A body of structured information describing some topic(s) of interest.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>schema:Dataset</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://schema.org/fileFormat">
    <rdfs:domain>
      <owl:Class rdf:nodeID="N224fe1e25c8848cc83915bd4c1b62692">
        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Dataset"/>
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Software"/>
        </owl:unionOf>
      </owl:Class>
    </rdfs:domain>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Media type, typically MIME format (see IANA site) of the content e.g. application/zip of a SoftwareApplication binary. In cases where a CreativeWork has several media type representations, 'encoding' can be used to indicate each MediaObject alongside particular fileFormat information. Unregistered or niche file formats can be indicated instead via the most appropriate URL, e.g. defining Web page or a Wikipedia entry.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>schema:fileFormat</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#associateFor">
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf>
      <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#directlySupports">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#supports"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The directlySupports property is a non-transitive version of supports, a subproperty of supports. directlySupports is a superproperty of created (inverse of createdBy), derivedTo (inverse of derivedFrom), associateFor (inverse of associatedWith), usedBy (inverse of used), and generated (inverse of generatedBy).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>directlySupports</rdfs:label>
      </owl:ObjectProperty>
    </rdfs:subPropertyOf>
    <owl:inverseOf>
      <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#associatedWith">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#directlySupportedBy"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Agent"/>
        <rdfs:comment>A prov:Agent that has some responsibility for the occurrence of this prov:Activity is associatedWith the prov:Activity.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>associatedWith</rdfs:label>
      </owl:ObjectProperty>
    </owl:inverseOf>
    <rdfs:comment>Reverse of associatedWith property.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>associateFor</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://schema.org/endTime">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Computation"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The endTime of something. For a reserved event or service (e.g. FoodEstablishmentReservation), the time that it is expected to end. For actions that span a period of time, when the action was performed. e.g. John wrote a book from January to December. For media, including audio and video, it's the time offset of the end of a clip within a larger file.

Note that Event uses startDate/endDate instead of startTime/endTime, even when describing dates with times. This situation may be clarified in future revisions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>schema:endTime</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#serviceUsedBy">
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#usedBy"/>
    <owl:inverseOf>
      <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#usedService">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#used"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Computation"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Service"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The property usedService is a subproperty of used where domain is Computation and range is Service.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>usedService</rdfs:label>
      </owl:ObjectProperty>
    </owl:inverseOf>
    <rdfs:comment>Reverse of usedService property.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>serviceUsedBy</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://schema.org/author">
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The author of the content.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>schema:author</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#generated">
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#directlySupports"/>
    <owl:inverseOf>
      <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#generatedBy">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#directlySupportedBy"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Generation is the completion of production of a new prov:Entity by a prov:Activity. This entity did not exist before generation and becomes available for usage after this generation.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>generatedBy</rdfs:label>
      </owl:ObjectProperty>
    </owl:inverseOf>
    <rdfs:comment>Reverse of generatedBy property.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>generated</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://schema.org/runtime">
    <rdfs:comment>Runtime platform or script interpreter dependencies (example: Java v1, Python 2.3, .NET Framework 3.0).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>schema:runtime</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://schema.org/title">
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The title of a Thing.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>schema:title</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Agent"/>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#DigitalObject"/>
    <rdfs:comment>An entity responsible for making the resource. Examples of a creator include a person, an organization, or a service i.e. a SoftwareAgent. Typically, the name of a creator should be used to indicate the entity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>terms:creator</rdfs:label>
  </owl:AnnotationProperty>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#indirectlyChallengedBy">
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#challengedBy"/>
    <owl:inverseOf>
      <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#indirectlyChallenges">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#challenges"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#DigitalObject"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#DigitalObject"/>
        <owl:propertyChainAxiom rdf:parseType="Collection">
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#directlyChallenges"/>
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#supports"/>
        </owl:propertyChainAxiom>
        <rdfs:comment>The indirectlyChallenges property establishes a relation between instances of DigitalObjects when one indirectly challenges the other entailed by property chaining.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>indirectlyChallenges</rdfs:label>
      </owl:ObjectProperty>
    </owl:inverseOf>
    <rdfs:comment>Reverse of indirectlyChallenges property.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>indirectlyChallengedBy</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://schema.org/SoftwareApplication">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Software"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A software application.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>schema:SoftwareApplication</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://schema.org/datePublished">
    <rdfs:domain>
      <owl:Class rdf:nodeID="Nae1fb5f4dc7c48cd976546d1348807e5">
        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Dataset"/>
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Software"/>
        </owl:unionOf>
      </owl:Class>
    </rdfs:domain>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Date when the item was first published.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>schema:datePublished</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Reference">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#DigitalObject"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A Reference is a bibliographic record. References are Representations which represent and attribute archived digital or bibliographic objects, including Articles, Datasets, and Software.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>Reference</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#hasSchema">
    <owl:inverseOf>
      <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#schemaFor">
        <rdfs:comment>Reverse of hasSchema property.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>schemaFor</rdfs:label>
      </owl:ObjectProperty>
    </owl:inverseOf>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Dataset"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Schema"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The hasSchema property describes the content-level schema of a Dataset.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>hasSchema</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#additionalDocumentation">
    <rdfs:domain>
      <owl:Class rdf:nodeID="N8d70fab71aa346369ab57092c14fd86c">
        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Computation"/>
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Dataset"/>
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Software"/>
        </owl:unionOf>
      </owl:Class>
    </rdfs:domain>
    <rdfs:range>
      <rdfs:Datatype rdf:nodeID="Nba18313217824cabb89eeaf2b9037aeb">
        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"/>
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        </owl:unionOf>
      </rdfs:Datatype>
    </rdfs:range>
    <rdfs:comment>Any additional information of the item that may be useful.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>additionalDocumentation</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://schema.org/Organization">
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Organization"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Agent"/>
    <rdfs:comment>An organization such as a school, NGO, corporation, club, etc.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>schema:Organization</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#derivedFrom">
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf>
      <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#directlySupportedBy">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#supportedBy"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#directlySupports"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The use of directlySupportedBy property is intended to establish a direct relation between instances of DigitalObjects.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>directlySupportedBy</rdfs:label>
      </owl:ObjectProperty>
    </rdfs:subPropertyOf>
    <owl:inverseOf>
      <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#derivedTo">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#directlySupports"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Reverse of derivedFrom property.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>derivedTo</rdfs:label>
      </owl:ObjectProperty>
    </owl:inverseOf>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A derivation is a transformation of a prov:Entity into another, an update of a prov:Entity resulting in a new one, or the construction of a new prov:Entity based on a pre-existing prov:Entity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>derivedFrom</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://schema.org/keywords">
    <rdfs:domain>
      <owl:Class rdf:nodeID="Nd9cc652321fc40218985666bd3e56e7d">
        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Computation"/>
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Dataset"/>
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Software"/>
        </owl:unionOf>
      </owl:Class>
    </rdfs:domain>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Keywords or tags used to describe some item. Multiple textual entries in a keywords list are typically delimited by commas, or by repeating the property.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>schema:keywords</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://schema.org/SoftwareSourceCode">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Software"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Computer programming source code. Example: Full (compile ready) solutions, code snippet samples, scripts, templates.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>schema:SoftwareSourceCode</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#representedBy">
    <owl:inverseOf>
      <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#represents">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#DigitalObject"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity"/>
        <rdfs:comment>A DigitalObject represents an Entity or any of its features or feature sets.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>represents</rdfs:label>
      </owl:ObjectProperty>
    </owl:inverseOf>
    <rdfs:comment>Reverse of represents property.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>representedBy</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#instrumentUsedBy">
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#usedBy"/>
    <owl:inverseOf>
      <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#usedInstrument">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#used"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Experiment"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Instrument"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The property usedInstrument is a subproperty of used where domain is Experiment and range is Instrument.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>usedInstrument</rdfs:label>
      </owl:ObjectProperty>
    </owl:inverseOf>
    <rdfs:comment>Reverse of usedInstrument property.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>instrumentUsedBy</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://schema.org/Claim">
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Claim"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#DigitalObject"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A Claim in Schema.org represents a specific, factually-oriented claim that could be the itemReviewed in a ClaimReview. The content of a claim can be summarized with the text property. Variations on well known claims can have their common identity indicated via sameAs links, and summarized with a name. Ideally, a Claim description includes enough contextual information to minimize the risk of ambiguity or inclarity. In practice, many claims are better understood in the context in which they appear or the interpretations provided by claim reviews.

Beyond ClaimReview, the Claim type can be associated with related creative works - for example a ScholaryArticle or Question might be about some Claim.

At this time, Schema.org does not define any types of relationship between claims. This is a natural area for future exploration.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>schema:Claim</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#modelFormat">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#MLModel"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The file format of the model (e.g., ONNX, HDF5, Pickle).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>modelFormat</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://schema.org/encodingFormat">
    <rdfs:domain>
      <owl:Class rdf:nodeID="N45bf685262704c1d85a894340ca8c506">
        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Dataset"/>
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Software"/>
        </owl:unionOf>
      </owl:Class>
    </rdfs:domain>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The format of the item in question encoded into.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>schema:encodingFormat</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#EvidenceGraph">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#DigitalObject"/>
    <rdfs:comment>An EvidenceGraph is a directed acyclic graph

Ev = (Rn, r+, r-)

where Rn is a set of DigitalObjects (and the Activities or Agents that warrant them), r+ is a set of supports relations, r- is a set of challenge relations, and r+ ∩ r- = ∅.

EvidenceGraphs are bipolar argumentation frameworks (Cayrol &amp; Lagasquie-Schiex, 2009) represented as RDF named graphs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>EvidenceGraph</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/terms/title"/>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#containedBy">
    <owl:inverseOf>
      <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#contains">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#TransitiveProperty"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#DigitalObject"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#DigitalObject"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Instances of DigitalObjects may contain instances of other DigitalObjects.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>contains</rdfs:label>
      </owl:ObjectProperty>
    </owl:inverseOf>
    <rdfs:comment>Reverse of contains property.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>containedBy</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://schema.org/license">
    <rdfs:domain>
      <owl:Class rdf:nodeID="Nb24708e6392840aa9ab2893dd300363f">
        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Dataset"/>
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Software"/>
        </owl:unionOf>
      </owl:Class>
    </rdfs:domain>
    <rdfs:range>
      <rdfs:Datatype rdf:nodeID="Ndc0d77a39158460484aad413bdbc341e">
        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"/>
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        </owl:unionOf>
      </rdfs:Datatype>
    </rdfs:range>
    <rdfs:comment>A license document that applies to this content, typically indicated by URL.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>schema:license</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://schema.org/dateModified">
    <rdfs:domain>
      <owl:Class rdf:nodeID="N4a6c8d772e294d5f8542f290611e631c">
        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Dataset"/>
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Software"/>
        </owl:unionOf>
      </owl:Class>
    </rdfs:domain>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The date when the item was last modified.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>schema:dateModified</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified"/>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://schema.org/name">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The name of the item.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>schema:name</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#inputSize">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#MLModel"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The expected input size or shape the model is designed to receive and process at one time. For example, image classification models such as ResNet, VGG commonly use 224x224 pixels with 3 channels while Language Models such as BERT, GPT use tokens or context length from thousand to millions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>inputSize</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#describedBy">
    <owl:inverseOf>
      <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#describes">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Method"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The describes property is used when a Method, generally composed with a block of text, narrates a prov:Activity that takes place.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>describes</rdfs:label>
      </owl:ObjectProperty>
    </owl:inverseOf>
    <rdfs:comment>Reverse of describes property.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>describedBy</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://schema.org/startTime">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Computation"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The startTime of something. For a reserved event or service (e.g. FoodEstablishmentReservation), the time that it is expected to start. For actions that span a period of time, when the action was performed. e.g. John wrote a book from January to December. For media, including audio and video, it's the time offset of the start of a clip within a larger file.

Note that Event uses startDate/endDate instead of startTime/endTime, even when describing dates with times. This situation may be clarified in future revisions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>schema:startTime</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#intendedUseCase">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#MLModel"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The context in which this model is intended to be used.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>intendedUseCase</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#softwareUsedBy">
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#usedBy"/>
    <owl:inverseOf>
      <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#usedSoftware">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#used"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Computation"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Software"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The property usedSoftware is a subproperty of used where domain is Computation and range is Software.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>usedSoftware</rdfs:label>
      </owl:ObjectProperty>
    </owl:inverseOf>
    <rdfs:comment>Reverse of usedSoftware property.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>softwareUsedBy</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#datasetUsedBy">
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#usedBy"/>
    <owl:inverseOf>
      <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#usedDataset">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#used"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Computation"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Dataset"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The property usedDataset is a subproperty of used where domain is Computation and range is Dataset.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>usedDataset</rdfs:label>
      </owl:ObjectProperty>
    </owl:inverseOf>
    <rdfs:comment>Reverse of usedDataset property.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>datasetUsedBy</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#created">
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#directlySupports"/>
    <owl:inverseOf>
      <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#createdBy">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#directlySupportedBy"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Agent"/>
        <rdfs:comment>A prov:Agent is a creator of a prov:Entity if it is createdBy the Agent.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>createdBy</rdfs:label>
      </owl:ObjectProperty>
    </owl:inverseOf>
    <rdfs:comment>Reverse of createdBy property.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>created</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#publicationVenue">
    <rdfs:domain>
      <owl:Class rdf:nodeID="Nb0c76f41823b4c879458e8d80a7b8911">
        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Dataset"/>
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Software"/>
        </owl:unionOf>
      </owl:Class>
    </rdfs:domain>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The (digital/physical) name where the item was published.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>publicationVenue</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://schema.org/contentSize">
    <rdfs:domain>
      <owl:Class rdf:nodeID="N8650cdda77fb4d1aa3b6bf828c8e5e61">
        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Dataset"/>
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Software"/>
        </owl:unionOf>
      </owl:Class>
    </rdfs:domain>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long"/>
    <rdfs:comment>File size in (tera/giga/mega/kilo) bytes.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>schema:contentSize</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#state">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Claim"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Textual representation of a claim</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>state</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://schema.org/Person">
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Person"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Agent"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A person (alive, dead, undead, or fictional).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>schema:Person</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#associatedPublication">
    <rdfs:domain>
      <owl:Class rdf:nodeID="N43ad46c4c2c149f1ac81c3eb55eaf901">
        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Computation"/>
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Dataset"/>
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Software"/>
        </owl:unionOf>
      </owl:Class>
    </rdfs:domain>
    <rdfs:range>
      <rdfs:Datatype rdf:nodeID="Nbb4663354eee4d05beb40f00e74106f9">
        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"/>
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        </owl:unionOf>
      </rdfs:Datatype>
    </rdfs:range>
    <rdfs:comment>Reference to the publications where the item or its relevant information can be discovered.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>associatedPublication</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#ROCrate">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Package"/>
    <rdfs:comment>An approach to packaging research data with their metadata.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>ROCrate</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Image">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Dataset"/>
    <rdfs:comment>An Image is a visual representation of structured or unstructured data produced digitally.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>Image</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#modelType">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#MLModel"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The type or category of the machine learning model (e.g., Classification, Regression, Generative).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>modelType</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#hasBias">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#MLModel"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Any issue of a model that may consistently deviate its outcome to be incorrect or unfair.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>hasBias</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#framework">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#MLModel"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The machine learning framework used to create the model (e.g., PyTorch, TensorFlow).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>framework</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/terms/license"/>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#sampleUsedBy">
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#usedBy"/>
    <owl:inverseOf>
      <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#usedSample">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#used"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Experiment"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Sample"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The property usedSample is a subproperty of used where domain is Experiment and range is Sample.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>usedSample</rdfs:label>
      </owl:ObjectProperty>
    </owl:inverseOf>
    <rdfs:comment>Reverse of usedSample property.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>sampleUsedBy</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://schema.org/Service">
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Service"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#SoftwareAgent"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A service provided by an organization, e.g. delivery service, print services, etc</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>schema:Service</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://schema.org/contentUrl">
    <owl:equivalentProperty>
      <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#contentUrl">
        <rdfs:domain>
          <owl:Class rdf:nodeID="Nb53b9ad744a446e691fa2c742fbd2364">
            <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
              <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Dataset"/>
              <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Software"/>
            </owl:unionOf>
          </owl:Class>
        </rdfs:domain>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The location or URL of the content.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>contentUrl</rdfs:label>
      </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    </owl:equivalentProperty>
    <rdfs:domain>
      <owl:Class rdf:nodeID="N1190cc29b8444837b7b84a1ffd8ed434">
        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Dataset"/>
          <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Software"/>
        </owl:unionOf>
      </owl:Class>
    </rdfs:domain>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Actual bytes of the object, for example the data file or image file or video file.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>schema:contentUrl</rdfs:label>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#annotates">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Annotation"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#DigitalObject"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The annotates property is used for annotating instances of DigitalObjects.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>annotates</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://schema.org/Article">
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Article"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Document"/>
    <rdfs:comment>An article, such as a news article or piece of investigative report. Newspapers and magazines have articles of many different types and this is intended to cover them all.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>schema:Article</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#packagedBy">
    <owl:inverseOf>
      <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#packages">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Container"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Software"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Instances of software can be packaged by the instances of containers.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>packages</rdfs:label>
      </owl:ObjectProperty>
    </owl:inverseOf>
    <rdfs:comment>Reverse of packages property.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>packagedBy</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#mlModelUsedBy">
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#usedBy"/>
    <owl:inverseOf>
      <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#usedMLModel">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#used"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Computation"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#MLModel"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The property usedMLModel is a subproperty of used where domain is Computation and range is MLModel. This is common in fine-tuning or inference tasks.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>usedMLModel</rdfs:label>
      </owl:ObjectProperty>
    </owl:inverseOf>
    <rdfs:comment>Reverse of usedMLModel property.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>mlModelUsedBy</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/terms/created"/>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionIRI"/>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/terms/description"/>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor"/>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespaceUri"/>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespacePrefix"/>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://swrl.stanford.edu/ontologies/3.3/swrla.owl#isRuleEnabled"/>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Container">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#DigitalObject"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A container is a digital object that can be defined as packages of software. Instances of containers are accompanied by all necessary dependencies such as specific versions, runtime environment and required libraries for execution.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>Container</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Service">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#SoftwareAgent"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A Service is a SoftwareAgent accessed online that executes a Computation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>Service</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#DigitalObject">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A DigitalObject is an Entity which represents another Entity. DigitalObjects are always attributedTo an Agent, their creator, contributor, influencer or to an Activity they were generatedBy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>DigitalObject</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Experiment">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity"/>
    <rdfs:comment>An experiment is an activity where samples are treated with reagents and analyzed using instruments.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>Experiment</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#used">
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#directlySupportedBy"/>
    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#usedBy"/>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity"/>
    <rdfs:comment>An Activity used an Entity, when the Entity (such as a Dataset or a Software) was instrumental in enabling that Activity to occur.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>used</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Dataset">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#DigitalObject"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A body of structured information describing some topic(s) of interest.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>Dataset</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Method">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#DigitalObject"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A descriptive recipe describing how a DigitalObject is made or obtained. It describes an Activity and may refer to other DigitalObjects or entities as components of the recipe.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>Method</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Person">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Agent"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A Person is a human Agent.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>prov:Person</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Article">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Document"/>
    <rdfs:comment>An Article is a (typically compound) textual document conveying a set of Claims and other DigitalObjects. Among these, an Article in EVI always conveys an assertion of its authorship in the form of a bibliographic self-reference.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>Article</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Instrument">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity"/>
    <rdfs:comment>An Instrument is an entity such as a tool, device or equipment that is used in an experiment to perform measurements or manipulations, observations, or other actions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>Instrument</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Organization">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Agent"/>
    <rdfs:comment>An Organization is a social or legal institution with structure and purpose such as a company, society, university, sports team, etc.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>prov:Organization</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#SoftwareAgent">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Agent"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A Service is considered a SoftwareAgent that can be invoked and executed. A Software is different from SoftwareAgent in the context that it can be downloaded.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>prov:SoftwareAgent</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Schema">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#DigitalObject"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A semi-structured interpretation of instances of DigitalObjects that can help comprehend the content.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>Schema</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#challenges">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#DigitalObject"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#DigitalObject"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The challenges property is entailed by property chain rule when a DigitalObject A either directly challenges another DigitalObject B, or indirectlyChallenges B by challenging a DigitalObject which supports it.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>challenges</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#MLModel">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#DigitalObject"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An MLModel is a computational model that has been trained on data to perform a specific task. It is a digital object that captures the learned parameters and architecture resulting from a machine learning training process (Computation).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">MLModel</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity">
    <rdfs:comment>An Activity is a process by which an Entity is produced, modified, consumed or used.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>prov:Activity</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#supportedBy">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#TransitiveProperty"/>
    <owl:inverseOf>
      <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#supports">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#TransitiveProperty"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The supports property is a transitive relation entailed by its non-transitive subproperty directlySupports. Typical nodes are DigitalObjects; provenance shortcuts (used, generatedBy, createdBy, associatedWith) also participate so warrant can propagate through Activities and Agents. If A supports B, the correctness of A is a warrant for belief in the correctness of B.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>supports</rdfs:label>
      </owl:ObjectProperty>
    </owl:inverseOf>
    <rdfs:comment>Inverse of supports. Transitive, matching supports.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>supportedBy</rdfs:label>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Package">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#DigitalObject"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Metadata associated with digital resources that may be packaged together or referenced.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>Package</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Software">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#DigitalObject"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Software is a specific set of computer-interpretable instructions to perform one or more Computations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>Software</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Agent">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity"/>
    <rdfs:comment>An Agent is an autonomous Entity. Persons and Organizations are Agents in EVI. Agents may be associatedWith Activities, and Entities may be attributedTo Agents.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>prov:Agent</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity">
    <rdfs:comment>An Entity is a physical, digital, conceptual, or other kind of thing with some fixed aspects.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>prov:Entity</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Document">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#DigitalObject"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A Document is a digital object that contains information intended for human or machine interpretation. As a DigitalObject, it represents any identifiable information resource that can be stored, transmitted, and referenced, serving as the foundational class for a more specific type such as an Annotation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>Document</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Sample">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A sample is an entity such as a biological/physical specimen or material that is being tested in an experiment.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>Sample</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Claim">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#DigitalObject"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A Claim is a declarative sentence or assertion. Claims are defeasible.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>Claim</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Annotation">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/EVI#Document"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Annotation is a Document that comments on or provides interpretability of an analysis. The analysis could be based on an LLM analysis (or any analysis) of a Computation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>Annotation</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Reagent">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A Reagent is an entity such as chemical substance or biological material that is used to initiate reactions in an experiment.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>Reagent</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/EVI#Computation">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Computation is an Activity performed on a Dataset with the help of a Software.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>Computation</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
</rdf:RDF>
